{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You are children, etc.</b> One needs to know the reason that the statement <b>you are children</b> is juxtaposed to the statement ״תִּתְגּוֹדְדוּ״ (you shall not gash yourselves)? It appears that the intention is to say that in the death of a person there is no loss for the deceased; rather, he is like a man who sent his son to trade in another city, and after some days the father sent for his son, and the son's absence is only from the place he departed from, but in any case he exists, and what is more, it is good for him, for the son returned to his father who is the source of life. And on this account we are not to gash ourselves and make a bald spot. Unlike the nations, who are not called children of HaShem — and this is what is said <b>you</b>, to exclude the other nations, over whom mourners wail on the day of their death, for they die a death such that they are no longer to be found among the living."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:23.478872831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}